module

public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.Limits.AlgebraSheafIdealQuotientLift
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.Limits.SurjectiveFinitePresentationSystem

/-!
# The system of quotients `ℬ_i/ℐ_i` approximating a quasi-coherent algebra on an algebraic space

Let `S` be a scheme, `X` an algebraic space over `S` and `𝒜` a quasi-coherent `𝒪_X`-algebra.
The proof of [Stacks, Tag 082A] approximates `𝒜` by the algebras

`𝒜_{i,j} = ℬ_i/ℐ_{i,j}`,   `ℬ_i = Sym(ℱ_i)`,   `ℐ_{i,j} ⊆ ℐ_i = ker(ℬ_i ⟶ 𝒜)`,

and this file builds that system: given a filtered system `ℬ` of algebra sheaves over `𝒜` and a
choice of ideal `ℐ_i` of each `ℬ_i` killed by `ℬ_i ⟶ 𝒜` and carried into `ℐ_j` by each
transition map, it constructs

* the diagram `i ↦ ℬ_i/ℐ_i` of algebra sheaves, whose transition maps are the factorizations of
  `ℬ_i ⟶ ℬ_j ⟶ ℬ_j/ℐ_j` through `ℬ_i ⟶ ℬ_i/ℐ_i`, and
* its cocone over `𝒜`, whose leg at `i` is the factorization of `ℬ_i ⟶ 𝒜` through
  `ℬ_i ⟶ ℬ_i/ℐ_i`,

and then concludes [Stacks, Tag 082A] by reindexing the filtered system by a directed poset.

What this adds to
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.Limits.SurjectiveFinitePresentationSystem`, whose Stacks
082A theorem carries the entire filtered system of finitely presented quasi-coherent algebras as
a hypothesis, is that **the members of the system and the morphisms between them are no longer
hypotheses**: they are built here, out of the quotient of an algebra sheaf by a sheaf of ideals
and its universal property
(`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.Limits.AlgebraSheafIdealQuotient` and
`...IdealQuotientLift`).  That quotient is the object whose absence at the level of algebraic
spaces was the recorded obstruction to the construction.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.idealQuotientSystem`: **the diagram `i ↦ ℬ_i/ℐ_i`.**
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.idealQuotientSystemCocone`: **its cocone over `𝒜`.**

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_directed_isFinitePresentation_algebra_of_idealQuotients`:
  **Stacks 082A over the system datum, the finiteness of its stages and the colimit property of
  the constructed cocone.**  The tag's clause lists exactly what is carried.

## Implementation notes

Functoriality of `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.idealQuotientSystem` and naturality of its cocone are
both proved by `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.AlgebraSheaf.idealQuotient_hom_ext`: two morphisms out of
`ℬ/ℐ` which agree after composition with `ℬ ⟶ ℬ/ℐ` are equal.  No computation with sections
appears, because every morphism out of a quotient in sight is a factorization and the
factorizations are determined by what they do on `ℬ`.

### What is carried, and why

Three things are hypotheses, and each is a separately identifiable missing ingredient rather
than the conclusion in disguise.

* The **system datum** `D`, `ψ`: a filtered system of algebra sheaves with a cocone over `𝒜`.
  In the source this is `ℬ_i = Sym(ℱ_i)` with the maps induced by a presentation
  `𝒜 = colim ℱ_i` of the underlying module ([Stacks, Tag 07V9]), and it is the one step of the
  source's construction that this tree still cannot take: the symmetric algebra of a module on
  an algebraic space exists, as `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.symmetricAlgebraSheaf`, but neither its
  functoriality in the module nor the *ungraded* universal property that produces the map
  `Sym(ℱ_i) ⟶ 𝒜` out of `ℱ_i ⟶ 𝒜` is available at the algebraic space level; both exist only
  for schemes, as `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.symmetricAlgebraSheafMap` and
  `Stacks.SymAlgSheaf.algebraLift`.  Quasi-coherence of `Sym` on an algebraic space is likewise
  unproved, being a hypothesis at every use site in
  `StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.NormalConeOfImmersion`.
* The **finiteness of the stages** `hstage`.  Quasi-coherence and finite presentation of
  `ℬ_i/ℐ_i` are conditions on its sections over the affine étale charts, and the sections of the
  quotient are the sheafification of `U ↦ ℬ_i(U)/ℐ_i(U)`, not that presheaf; identifying the two
  over an affine chart is a vanishing statement for the first cohomology of `ℐ_i` there, which
  this tree does not have for the small étale site of an algebraic space.  In the source this is
  where `ℐ_{i,j}` being generated by a *finite type* submodule enters, and that is why the
  ideals here are arbitrary: no use is made of finite generation, so none is asked for.
* The **colimit property** `hcol` of the constructed cocone.  Colimits in
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.AlgebraSheaf` are not constructed anywhere in this tree -- the
  category is a bespoke structure rather than an `Under` category, so the scheme-level route of
  `Stacks.RelativeSpec.AlgebraSheaf.isColimit_of_isColimit_forget` is unavailable -- and the
  scheme-level criterion that reduces it to two conditions on sections over affine opens,
  `Stacks.QcohAlgebraFPColimit.nonempty_isColimit_of_affineSections`, is stated for schemes.

Quasi-compactness and quasi-separatedness of `X` do **not** appear.  They are not dropped from
the content: in the source they are used only to produce the system datum `D`, `ψ` through
Stacks 07V9, and that datum is a hypothesis here, so the statement below is the source's with
those two hypotheses replaced by their consequence.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 082A](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/082A)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07V9](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07V9)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Space

variable {B : BigFppfSite.{u}} {S : Scheme.{u}} {hS : B.Contains S}
    {X : (BigFppfOver B S hS)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u} {hX : IsAlgebraicSpace B S hS X}

section System

variable {P : Type u} [SmallCategory P] (A : AlgebraSheaf.{u, u} B S hS X hX)
    (D : P ⥤ AlgebraSheaf.{u, u} B S hS X hX) (ψ : D ⟶ (Functor.const P).obj A)
    (I : ∀ p : P, (D.obj p).IdealSheaf)
    (hkill : ∀ (p : P) (U : (SmallEtale B S hS X)ᵒᵖ) (a : (D.obj p).right.obj.obj U),
      a ∈ (I p).obj U → ((ψ.app p).right.hom.app U).hom a = 0)
    (hmap : ∀ {p q : P} (g : p ⟶ q) (U : (SmallEtale B S hS X)ᵒᵖ)
      (a : (D.obj p).right.obj.obj U),
      a ∈ (I p).obj U → ((D.map g).right.hom.app U).hom a ∈ (I q).obj U)

/-- The transition map `ℬ_p/ℐ_p ⟶ ℬ_q/ℐ_q` of the system: the factorization through
`ℬ_p ⟶ ℬ_p/ℐ_p` of the composite `ℬ_p ⟶ ℬ_q ⟶ ℬ_q/ℐ_q`, which kills `ℐ_p` because the
transition map of `ℬ` carries `ℐ_p` into `ℐ_q`. -/
def idealQuotientTransition {p q : P} (g : p ⟶ q) :
    (D.obj p).idealQuotient (I p) ⟶ (D.obj q).idealQuotient (I q) :=
  AlgebraSheaf.idealQuotientLift (D.map g ≫ (D.obj q).toIdealQuotient (I q)) (I p)
    fun U a ha =>
      AlgebraSheaf.toIdealQuotient_apply_eq_zero (D.obj q) (I q) U _ (hmap g U a ha)

/-- The transition map `ℬ_p/ℐ_p ⟶ ℬ_q/ℐ_q` composed with `ℬ_p ⟶ ℬ_p/ℐ_p` is the composite
`ℬ_p ⟶ ℬ_q ⟶ ℬ_q/ℐ_q`. -/
theorem toIdealQuotient_comp_idealQuotientTransition {p q : P} (g : p ⟶ q) :
    (D.obj p).toIdealQuotient (I p) ≫ idealQuotientTransition D I hmap g =
      D.map g ≫ (D.obj q).toIdealQuotient (I q) :=
  AlgebraSheaf.toIdealQuotient_comp_idealQuotientLift _ _ _

/-- **The diagram `i ↦ ℬ_i/ℐ_i` of algebra sheaves on `X`.**  Its members are the quotients of
the members of `D` by the chosen ideals, and its transition maps are the factorizations of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.idealQuotientTransition`.  Both functor laws are
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.AlgebraSheaf.idealQuotient_hom_ext`. -/
def idealQuotientSystem : P ⥤ AlgebraSheaf.{u, u} B S hS X hX where
  obj p := (D.obj p).idealQuotient (I p)
  map {_ _} g := idealQuotientTransition D I hmap g
  map_id p := by
    refine AlgebraSheaf.idealQuotient_hom_ext ?_
    rw [toIdealQuotient_comp_idealQuotientTransition, Category.comp_id, D.map_id,
      Category.id_comp]
  map_comp {p q r} g h := by
    refine AlgebraSheaf.idealQuotient_hom_ext ?_
    rw [toIdealQuotient_comp_idealQuotientTransition, ← Category.assoc,
      toIdealQuotient_comp_idealQuotientTransition, Category.assoc,
      toIdealQuotient_comp_idealQuotientTransition, D.map_comp, Category.assoc]

/-- The member of `idealQuotientSystem` at `p` is the quotient `ℬ_p/ℐ_p`. -/
@[simp]
theorem idealQuotientSystem_obj (p : P) :
    (idealQuotientSystem D I hmap).obj p = (D.obj p).idealQuotient (I p) :=
  rfl

/-- The transition map of `idealQuotientSystem` along `g` is `idealQuotientTransition`. -/
theorem idealQuotientSystem_map {p q : P} (g : p ⟶ q) :
    (idealQuotientSystem D I hmap).map g = idealQuotientTransition D I hmap g :=
  rfl

/-- **The cocone of the system `i ↦ ℬ_i/ℐ_i` over `𝒜`.**  Its leg at `i` is the factorization of
`ψ_i : ℬ_i ⟶ 𝒜` through `ℬ_i ⟶ ℬ_i/ℐ_i`, available because `ℐ_i` is killed by `ψ_i`. -/
def idealQuotientSystemCocone :
    idealQuotientSystem D I hmap ⟶ (Functor.const P).obj A where
  app p := AlgebraSheaf.idealQuotientLift (ψ.app p) (I p) (hkill p)
  naturality p q g := by
    refine AlgebraSheaf.idealQuotient_hom_ext ?_
    calc (D.obj p).toIdealQuotient (I p) ≫ idealQuotientTransition D I hmap g ≫
            AlgebraSheaf.idealQuotientLift (ψ.app q) (I q) (hkill q)
        = ((D.obj p).toIdealQuotient (I p) ≫ idealQuotientTransition D I hmap g) ≫
            AlgebraSheaf.idealQuotientLift (ψ.app q) (I q) (hkill q) :=
          (Category.assoc _ _ _).symm
      _ = (D.map g ≫ (D.obj q).toIdealQuotient (I q)) ≫
            AlgebraSheaf.idealQuotientLift (ψ.app q) (I q) (hkill q) :=
          congrArg (fun k : D.obj p ⟶ (D.obj q).idealQuotient (I q) =>
              k ≫ AlgebraSheaf.idealQuotientLift (ψ.app q) (I q) (hkill q))
            (toIdealQuotient_comp_idealQuotientTransition D I hmap g)
      _ = D.map g ≫ ((D.obj q).toIdealQuotient (I q) ≫
            AlgebraSheaf.idealQuotientLift (ψ.app q) (I q) (hkill q)) := Category.assoc _ _ _
      _ = D.map g ≫ ψ.app q :=
          congrArg (fun k : D.obj q ⟶ A => D.map g ≫ k)
            (AlgebraSheaf.toIdealQuotient_comp_idealQuotientLift (ψ.app q) (I q) (hkill q))
      _ = ψ.app p ≫ ((Functor.const P).obj A).map g := ψ.naturality g
      _ = ((D.obj p).toIdealQuotient (I p) ≫
            AlgebraSheaf.idealQuotientLift (ψ.app p) (I p) (hkill p)) ≫
            ((Functor.const P).obj A).map g :=
          congrArg (fun k : D.obj p ⟶ A => k ≫ ((Functor.const P).obj A).map g)
            (AlgebraSheaf.toIdealQuotient_comp_idealQuotientLift (ψ.app p) (I p) (hkill p)).symm
      _ = (D.obj p).toIdealQuotient (I p) ≫
            (AlgebraSheaf.idealQuotientLift (ψ.app p) (I p) (hkill p) ≫
              ((Functor.const P).obj A).map g) := Category.assoc _ _ _

/-- The leg at `p` of `idealQuotientSystemCocone`, composed with `ℬ_p ⟶ ℬ_p/ℐ_p`, is `ψ_p`. -/
theorem toIdealQuotient_comp_idealQuotientSystemCocone (p : P) :
    (D.obj p).toIdealQuotient (I p) ≫ (idealQuotientSystemCocone A D ψ I hkill hmap).app p =
      ψ.app p :=
  AlgebraSheaf.toIdealQuotient_comp_idealQuotientLift _ _ _

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 082A, over the system datum.**  Let `S` be a scheme, `X` an algebraic
space over `S` and `𝒜` an `𝒪_X`-algebra.  Let `D` be a filtered system of `𝒪_X`-algebras with a
cocone `ψ` over `𝒜`, and for each `i` let `ℐ_i` be a sheaf of ideals of `D_i` killed by `ψ_i`
and carried into `ℐ_j` by every transition map.  If every quotient `D_i/ℐ_i` is quasi-coherent
of finite presentation and the constructed cocone of those quotients over `𝒜` is colimiting,
then `𝒜` is the colimit of a system of quasi-coherent `𝒪_X`-algebras of finite presentation
indexed by a directed poset.

The members of the system and the morphisms between them are *constructed*: they are
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.idealQuotientSystem` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.idealQuotientSystemCocone`, built from the quotient of an algebra sheaf
by a sheaf of ideals and its universal property.  See the module documentation for what each of
the three hypotheses is and why it is a separate missing ingredient rather than the conclusion. -/
@[stacks 082A "PARTIAL, but the construction and not the reindexing: the members A_{i,j} = \
B_i/I_{i,j} of the source's system and the morphisms between them are constructed here, as \
quotients of an algebra sheaf on an algebraic space by a sheaf of ideals and factorizations \
through them, which is the object whose absence was the recorded obstruction. Three inputs are \
carried, each separately identified. (1) The system datum D, psi -- in the source B_i = \
Sym(F_i) with the maps induced by Stacks 07V9 -- because at the algebraic space level this tree \
has the symmetric algebra of a module but neither its functoriality in the module nor the \
ungraded universal property giving Sym(F_i) to A, both of which exist only for schemes \
(AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.symmetricAlgebraSheafMap, Stacks.SymAlgSheaf.algebraLift), \
nor quasi-coherence of Sym. (2) Quasi-coherence and finite presentation of each stage, which \
are conditions on the sections of a sheafification over the affine etale charts; this is where \
the source's finite generation of I_{i,j} is used, so the ideals here are arbitrary. (3) The \
colimit property of the constructed cocone, colimits in \
AlgebraicGeometry.Space.AlgebraSheaf being constructed nowhere in this tree. The source's \
quasi-compactness and quasi-separatedness are absent because they are used only to produce the \
system datum, which is hypothesis (1)"]
theorem exists_directed_isFinitePresentation_algebra_of_idealQuotients [IsFiltered P]
    (hstage : ∀ p : P, ((D.obj p).idealQuotient (I p)).IsQuasicoherent ∧
      ((D.obj p).idealQuotient (I p)).IsFinitePresentation)
    (hcol : IsColimit (Cocone.mk A (idealQuotientSystemCocone A D ψ I hkill hmap))) :
    ∃ (J : Type u) (_ : PartialOrder J) (_ : Nonempty J) (_ : IsDirected J (· ≤ ·))
      (E : J ⥤ AlgebraSheaf.{u, u} B S hS X hX) (φ : E ⟶ (Functor.const J).obj A)
      (_ : IsColimit (Cocone.mk A φ)),
      ∀ j, (E.obj j).IsQuasicoherent ∧ (E.obj j).IsFinitePresentation := by
  let _ : FinallySmall.{u} P := finallySmall_of_essentiallySmall.{u, u, u} P
  exact Stacks.DirectedCokernelSystem.exists_directed_of_filtered_colimit
    (fun C : AlgebraSheaf.{u, u} B S hS X hX => C.IsQuasicoherent ∧ C.IsFinitePresentation)
    (idealQuotientSystem D I hmap) A (idealQuotientSystemCocone A D ψ I hkill hmap) hcol hstage

end System

end AlgebraicGeometry.Space

end
